# Vantage Movers Business Logic

Business behavior changes must update this file or a linked business/workflow doc with the concept, source of truth, invariants, edge cases, and examples. If no update is needed, say so in the final response.

**Service docs:** `.cursor/businesslogic/` — per-service compact rules (form lead, call lead, RingCentral qualification, agent allocation, catalog, customers, testimonials, analytics, bookings, cancellations, …).

## Leads And Customers

- MongoDB is the system of record for form leads, call leads, customers, bookings, cancellations, and sync metadata.
- Form leads originate from website intake and may post to Granot CRM unless duplicate logic forces `post_to_granot=false`.
- Call leads originate from phone/call sources such as RingCentral/Invoca and may be enriched later from CRM rows.
- Customers are upserted from source leads or booking contact overrides during booking flows (`customer.service.md`); manual CRUD is separate.
- Extension/admin read paths: scored form search + call OR-search + paginated browse (`formLeadSearch.service.md`, `callLeadSearch.service.md`, `leadBrowse.service.md`); admin global search is separate (`adminSearch.service.md`).

## Quotes, Estimates, And Pricing

- `quoted`, `cubic_feet`, `est_cf`, CPL, deposit, total binder amount, and threshold flags appear across lead, enrichment, booking, and reporting flows.
- Source of truth and full pricing invariants are TBD from source of truth.

## Moves, Bookings, And Jobs

- Bookings link to a source lead via `lead_ref` and `lead_model` (`FormLead` or `CallLead`) except referral bookings (`is_referral_booking`, no lead link). See `businesslogic/bookings.service.md`.
- Booking creation can attach by direct Mongo id or source-derived identifiers such as form lead id, call job number, or call phone number.
- One lead-attached booking per `(lead_ref, lead_model)`; repeat creates upsert unless `submission_id` matches (idempotent no-op).
- Booking services mirror state back to source leads and schedule related Google Sheet sync work (`booking_chain` or referral `booked_lead` job).

## Cancellations

- Cancellations attach to lead-attached bookings only; referral bookings are blocked (409). See `businesslogic/cancelledLead.service.md`.
- Create resolves booking via `booked_lead` and/or `lead_id`, snapshots agent/job/source/customer fields, sets `booking.cancelled`, mirrors `cancelled` onto the source lead, and enqueues `cancellation_chain` sheet sync.
- Delete unwinds booking + lead refs and refreshes booked/source sheet rows before removing the cancellation document.
- Lead mirror semantics (`booked` retained alongside `cancelled`): `businesslogic/cancellationMirror.service.md`.

## Crews, Trucks, Dispatch, And Availability

- Agent and merchant reference data live in Mongo catalog collections; admin CRUD and active-name resolution: `catalog.service.md`.
- Agent allocations are required on booked leads and are resolved/snapshotted during booking (`agentAllocation.service.md`: active catalog lookup, 50/50 split, patch/replace, primary agent = index 0).
- Crew, truck, dispatch, route, and availability rules are TBD from source of truth.

## Invoices And Payments

- Booking records include merchant/deposit/binder-related fields. Invoice and payment lifecycle rules are TBD from source of truth.

## Integrations And CRM

- Granot CRM receives non-duplicate form leads and uses Mongo ids as `ref_no`/`leadno` for extension lookup.
- Google Sheets is an owner-facing reporting target; sheet sync can complete after API responses (`businesslogic/sheetSync.service.md`: outbox, Vercel Queue wake-up, drainer, `sheet_sync_jobs` collection).
- RingCentral call-lead qualification and promotion: webhook + Call Log cron → shared ingest (`ringcentral-call-lead-qualification.service.md`). Analytics reconcile is count-only and must not create leads.
- Granot Booked Jobs CSV reconciliation refreshes existing call leads and bookings from CRM rows without creating bookings (`bookedCallLeadReconciliation.service.md`).
- Marketing testimonials are read from Mongo via `testimonial.service.md`; the website fetches `published=true` reviews (ingest is ops/scripts, not API CRUD).
- Postman tooling syncs API collections/environments. External integration writes must remain mode-aware and observable.

## Invariants And Edge Cases

- Preserve traceability from website or call source through CRM, Mongo, Sheets, booking, cancellation, and reporting.
- Keep routes thin and business decisions in services.
- Do not bypass helpers for source-company parsing, phone normalization, local/CPL derivation, agent allocation resolution, duplicate/form-fill checks, or sheet-sync scheduling.
- Duplicates, unmatched call bookings, cancellations, historical database reads, and production backfills are high-risk and need focused tests or explicit validation notes.
